Return:
- title: a short test name.
- hypothesis: three parts - if_change (the change), then_outcome (the measurable effect on the primary metric), because (the evidence-based reason).
- variants: exactly {{ n_treatments }} treatment arm(s); each with a name, a description precise enough for a developer, and a list of concrete changes (element, old copy, new copy, styling).
- targeting: audiences, exclusions (internal traffic, bots ...), geo and any page conditions.
- metrics: one primary metric, 1-3 secondary metrics and at least one guardrail metric (role "guardrail", direction "no_harm"), each with a snake_case analytics event and a one-line definition.
- risks: 3-5 risks specific to this test, each with likelihood and mitigation.
- assumptions: the critical assumptions that must hold for the result to be valid.
